  "scope": "Actual routed material feeds local alternating end attachment. Formed chains cleave with internal links retained; the same attachment law reconstructs both fragments. Any finite number of repeated rounds is realized with explicit shared material and work budgets, without graph assignment or stock resetting. Failure retains partial structures and unused tokens. End-compatibility, size-eight cleavage, operation order, supplied building material and a structural input correspondence remain local premises. No force law, autonomous feed production, heritable variation in the organizing law, calendar-time growth rate, biological calibration or comparative superiority is proved."
}
